    "created_at": "2016-05-20T16:52:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-20T16:52:21Z",
    "body": "Mutation observers has this model too (only invoke when the stack is empty, which indeed has the difference between a user click and `click()`). What makes mutation observers special is that each mutation doesn't queue a microtask. But we handle a whole bunch of them in a single one, a compound microtask.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
