    "created_at": "2016-05-20T17:08:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-20T17:08:15Z",
    "body": "> This means that when the user clicks, microtasks happen after every click listener (since there is no code on the stack below each click listener); but when the page does el.click(), microtasks do not happen until the stack fully unwinds.\n\nYes, microtasks were very much designed to behave this way.\n\nAnd microtaks don't run during alert/confirm/prompt/etc. In Gecko, given the event loop model we have currently, this works usually, but once you start playing with multiple tabs, things may go wrong.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
